      "message": "Using this new `DECLARE_TRACE_EVENT()` by itself doesn\u0027t create a trace event. It was added so the regular `TRACE_EVENT()` macro could declare the trace function without the new `_tp` suffix.\n\nThat is my analysis of Steven\u0027s changes. Note that I also checked that none of the trace_android_vh_* functions got exposed to userspace under `/sys/kernel/tracing/events`.\n\nMaybe a name different naming of `DECLARE_TRACE_EVENT()` could have avoided the mixup? I guess this macro is only intended to be used by `TRACE_EVENT()` and thus the naming.\n\nThis is the only way that I found to keep the status quo for vendor hooks in a simple way. I don\u0027t know that reverting Steven\u0027s commit is feasible, as we would need to revert or modify several patches that now depend on this new behavior.",
